Is it escape that jumping is a member of?  Once you know
the jumping spell, use it for all room travel until you
have advanced that school to the maximum.

On advancing skills, pick your weapons ones *very* carefully.
Do NOT advance a weapon skill unless you can explain what
spell skill it will cost you and what problems that will
mean in the later game.  Wizards get enough to advance
every spell skill to max, dagger to Expert to be able to
machine gun 3 highly enchanted elven daggers per round (and
to use Magicbane face to face), and then only have a couple
of extras for any other weapon skill.  Think carefully
before enhancing quarterstaff, bare handed, some random
slot because you got an artifact.  Enhance the one good
other artifact you got once, and stick with it from then
on.  Ignore the rest without good reason.  On that, consider
the recent thread "Fun with polearms" for how to clear or
the two forts, but realistically consider that as a way to
spend your last two slots and only after all of the spell
ones and only as a why to train yourself to not advance
saber just because you got Werebane.


